      "message": "@fmalita, can you PTAL when you have a chance?\n\nThis CL fixes a bug that affects not only SkPngRustCodec, but also the older, `libpng`-based `SkPngCodec` (since `SkPngCodecBase` was extracted by me from `SkPngCodec` in a series of CLs starting with http://review.skia.org/893460) as well as `SkBmpCodec` (since it also uses `SkSwizzler`).\n\nI am quite confident in the fix based on the newly added PNG tests.  The `plte_trns.png` tests only go through `SkCodecPriv::ChoosePackColorProc` but they do *not* go through `applyColorXform`.  The `pltr_trns_gama.png` tests also go through `SkCodecPriv::ChoosePackColorProc` (after this CL without alpha premul) and *also* they go through `applyColorXform`.  And for both test inputs we ask for premul/unpremul output and rgba-vs-bgra output.  I created the test inputs using existing test utils from the `png` Rust crate + ad-hoc code to stitch them together in a new way.  I looked at the resulting files in a binary editor to confirm they look okay.\n\nI spent 20-30 minutes trying to read ImageMagick docs, but I was sadly unable to create a BMP test input (we need a BMP that uses 1) a palette and 2) alpha channel).  I think this is okay - things seems like they should work based on reading the code.\n\n/cc @danieldilan as FYI",
